# THE SHELF IS THE FRONT DOOR, not the forge. forge.php is a twenty-question
# interview; landing on it is right when somebody chose to build a world and
# wrong every other time, and "every other time" is almost every time once a
# person has one. router.php says the same thing to `php -S`, which does not
# read this file.
DirectoryIndex play.php forge.php
Options -Indexes

# NOT ONE OF THESE DENIALS IS CONDITIONAL ON ANYTHING. They were RewriteRules
# inside an <IfModule>, which makes a protection advice: a host that has never
# loaded mod_rewrite, or an AllowOverride that stops short of FileInfo, skips the
# whole block in silence — no error, no log line, just a docroot handing out its
# own source. The expression parser and mod_authz_core are part of the server
# itself, so these hold whatever else is or is not installed. <If> needs
# AllowOverride All where a RewriteRule needed FileInfo, and that is the trade
# worth making: too little AllowOverride now refuses every request in this
# directory with a 500 instead of quietly serving the files below.
#
# Every pattern is anchored (^|/) rather than ^ so it still holds when the app is
# deployed under a subdirectory, and closed (/|$) rather than $ so trailing
# PATH_INFO cannot walk past it. Both directions of a wrong guess here deny more
# than intended, never less.

# The engine and the forge library are deployed under lib/ so the docroot holds
# one self-contained tree (see boot.php). They are includes, not pages: nothing
# under lib/ is ever a URL — a .json fixture there is no more a URL than a .php
# file is, so this covers the whole tree rather than a list of extensions.
<If "%{REQUEST_URI} =~ m#(^|/)lib/#">
  Require all denied
</If>

# worker.php is the build itself, started by build.php over a pipe with the
# user's API key on its stdin. tick-worker.php is the same shape for the play
# view's time control. reroll-worker.php is the review step's re-run of one forge
# pass, addchar-worker.php writes one new person into a running world, and
# panel-worker.php puts a proposal to a discussion room. photo-worker.php is the reaper that develops a world's
# photographs, and story-worker.php writes a mystery over a
# running town. All
# six are CLI programs that happen to live here.
<If "%{REQUEST_URI} =~ m#(^|/)(worker|tick-worker|reroll-worker|addchar-worker|photo-worker|story-worker|panel-worker|heart|router)\.php(/|$)#">
  Require all denied
</If>

# The libraries: page chrome, the engine's front door, and the demo layer
# (identity, the caps, the model queue). Includes, never URLs — they define
# functions and print nothing, so fetching one is always a mistake.
#
# config.local.php is here for a different reason: it is the one file in this
# directory whose CONTENTS matter. It emits nothing when executed, so it is
# harmless while PHP handles .php — and it holds local_base, data_dir and the
# php path the moment PHP stops.
<If "%{REQUEST_URI} =~ m#(^|/)(boot|ui|play-lib|review-lib|why-lib|session|limits|queue|pdf|config\.local)\.php(/|$)#">
  Require all denied
</If>

# The test suite is not deployed at all (deploy.sh), but a docroot that ever
# acquires one must not serve it.
<If "%{REQUEST_URI} =~ m#(^|/)tests/#">
  Require all denied
</If>

# progress.php is the live stream — the build's and the time control's both.
# Nothing between here and the browser may sit on it waiting for more bytes, and
# nothing may cache it.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <Files ~ "^(build|progress)\.php$">
    Header always set X-Accel-Buffering "no"
    Header always set Cache-Control "no-cache, no-store, no-transform"
  </Files>
</IfModule>
<IfModule mod_deflate.c>
  <Files ~ "^(build|progress)\.php$">
    SetEnv no-gzip 1
    SetEnv dont-vary 1
  </Files>
</IfModule>
